---
scope: src/lib/utils/readFileHistory
alignment: unreviewed
description: The shared reader of the repository's version history, answering for any file when it was first added, when it last changed and which commit last touched it.
intent: >
  Page dates and doc commit links both depend on the repository's version
  history. This module reads that history once per build and answers, for any
  file in the repository, when it was first added (following renames back to
  its original name), when it last changed and the short id of its last
  commit. A file with no committed history gets no answers, never guessed or
  blank ones. Failures to read history surface to the caller. Paths match
  regardless of separator style or drive-letter case; a path outside the
  repository is an error.
outcomes:
  desired:
    - A build reads version history once, however many files it asks about.
    - First-added follows a file's renames back to its original name, and a file deleted and re-added reports its oldest add.
    - Last-changed and last commit match the newest commit that touched the file.
    - A file with no committed history gets no answers; they are absent, never empty or guessed.
    - The same file asked about twice in one build gives the same answer.
    - Paths with spaces or non-English characters are answered like any other path.
  undesired:
    - History is read once per file asked about instead of once per build.
    - A failed or overflowing history read returns empty answers instead of an error.
    - A date is taken from the build clock or a file's timestamps instead of its version history.
    - A path outside the repository is silently answered instead of rejected.
---
